tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2514-an-empty-group-record-names-every-route.hero:11:5: error[empty_record]: `partial` names only SOME of the header's fields, so a `partial` `record` with none names nothing — where the header's type is a struct, give the record the fields the program reads; where the header keeps the struct to itself, a `tag` and no fields make a HANDLE, C's pointer to it: `record Db tag sqlite3` is C's `sqlite3 *`; and where the type is a number, `typedef uint32_t mask_t;`, no record holds it: bind the number, `u32`, and `@mask: u32` where C takes a pointer to it
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2514-an-empty-group-record-names-every-route.hero:12:5: error[empty_record]: a `record` needs at least one field, indented one level below it — where the header's type is a struct, give the record the fields the program reads; where the header keeps the struct to itself, a `tag` and no fields make a HANDLE, C's pointer to it: `record Db tag sqlite3` is C's `sqlite3 *`; and where the type is a number, `typedef uint32_t mask_t;`, no record holds it: bind the number, `u32`, and `@mask: u32` where C takes a pointer to it
